---
/*
  Auswahl als Positionierung, mit dem zweiten Einstieg fuer die Creatorin, die
  ein Konto verloren hat, im gleichen Gewicht.
  04-konzept.md Abschnitt 4.3, Seite "/who-we-work-with", und Abschnitt 3.
  Die internen Ausschluesse (Profi-Darstellerinnen, Medienvertraege) bleiben
  bewusst von dieser Seite fern. Sie gehoeren in die Qualifizierung.

  Geaendert 08.09.2026: der Name der Fan-Plattform steht nirgends mehr, Ansage Manuel,
  Grund Banken. Ersatz: "your fan page". Jeder Abschnitt hat ein Bild.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import Split from '../components/Split.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Who we work with | Wunder"
  description="What we look for, in public, and what we do when you have lost an account before."
>
  <Split
    image="creator-speaking.webp"
    alt="A creator sits at a microphone and talks. She uses her hands while she explains something."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="We would rather say no early than waste your afternoon."
    eager
  >
    <h1>We say no more often than yes.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Here is what we look at. Check yourself against it, before you spend twenty minutes on a
      call.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Steady reach, not a follower count. Last month counts more than three years of collecting.</li>
      <li>A live fan page link that is yours.</li>
      <li>Content in English.</li>
      <li>A face people can see. We do not run an AI persona.</li>
      <li>Reach you did not buy.</li>
      <li>You pay tax in the European Union.</li>
      <li>Time for the posting rhythm we agree on. This is the one we say no over most.</li>
    </ul>
    <CtaBlock />
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="creator-checkin.webp"
    alt="A creator and Lauris sit at a podcast table with a Wunder sign behind them."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="Most creators we work with had an agency before us."
    flip
  >
    <h2>If you have lost an account before.</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      You are not starting at zero. You are building back an account that worked once. This time
      you can see every step we take.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some of those earlier agencies were bad. That is not a no here. We want to know the history
      of the account. We want to know how you lost it. We would rather hear both at the start than
      in month three.
    </p>
    <p>
      Maybe your last month was quiet because you stopped posting. Say so in the form. It changes
      the plan, not the answer.
    </p>
    <CtaBlock />
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="lauris-speaking.webp"
    alt="Lauris sits at a microphone and explains something to the person across the table."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="A clear no now saves both of us three months."
  >
    <h2>Who we do not take on.</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Anyone who pays tax outside the European Union. We cannot pay you the way we pay the rest.</li>
      <li>
        Anyone still tied to another agency or manager, until that deal ends. See <a
          href="/switching">switching</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>Accounts with reach that was bought.</li>
      <li>Faceless accounts and AI personas.</li>
      <li>Anyone who wants us to run the account alone. There is no version of this without you.</li>
    </ul>
  </Split>
</Base>
